  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Operational and Logistical Support to COVID Vaccination Campaign</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Given its footprint in country and intrinsic knowledge of population movements and dynamics in country, as well as its experience in facilitating largescale and complex logistical operations in areas of high displacement, IOM is supporting the Government of Chad in the roll out of the national vaccination campaign specifically for mobile and displaced populations in parallel in the Moyen Chari, Logone Oriental, Logone Occidentale, Lac, Borkou, Ennedi, and Tibesti provincesSpecifically, IOM supports the Government in rolling-out the national vaccination campaign against COVID-19 for mobile and displaced communities in three consecutive phases across the seven above-mentioned provinces :1) Phase 1 &#x2013; Community outreach on COVID-19 prevention and vaccination to ensure readiness and acceptance of the vaccine2) Phase 2 &#x2013; Logistical support to the facilitation of the vaccination campaign3) Phase 3&#x2013; Management of a feedback mechanism through a hotline, quality monitoring and referral mechanisms for any secondary effects.</narrative>
  </description>
